From 5e7fac16bfb6bc0e82951e2ed507e1eaac66fa07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 18:01:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-11: zoom the design surface with Ctrl+wheel (WPF),
 25%..400% (0.11.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- CSS zoom on <body> only; the overlay lives on <html>, so boxes, handles and
  snaplines stay in viewport px and line up with the zoomed page
- every screen delta (drag, resize, align) is divided by the zoom before it
  becomes a CSS px value in the source; arrow keys stay 1 / 10 page px; the
  size on the label is the page's px, not the screen's
- zoom shown on the badge and the status bar, kept per page across reloads;
  "HT9045: 設計檢視縮放回 100%" resets it

Tests: probe 2 pages x 22 asserted (200%: a 20px drag writes +10px; Ctrl+wheel
steps 2 -> 3) + all layers; a 150% screenshot checked by eye (box and handles
on the input, the second selection boxed).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
